<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Chapter 57 — Service Mesh.
    mesh/       SpiffeId (workload identities in URI SANs) and Sidecar (Envoy bootstrap configurations: an outbound
                listener balancing each request across a headless Service's pods, with retries, outlier detection and
                mTLS; an inbound listener that requires mTLS and admits only listed identities)
  verify/run.sh validates every configuration with Envoy 1.39.4, then runs Envoy sidecars (native sidecar containers)
  on a real cluster (k3s 1.37): per-request balancing after a scale-out, who can reach a service, a bad pod with
  retries and outlier detection, and the latency and resources a sidecar costs.
-->
